Normalizations: NZ-01 (scratch /tmp/hde-crd-0002-qa18), NZ-06 (publication helper), NZ-25 (the Plan's request lines written as curl --http1.1 commands; HEAD -I; OPTIONS/DELETE/POST -X; bodies --data-binary; --path-as-is for //reader).
Observation rows o1 (OPTIONS /dev/sampler/conjunction) and o2 (GET //reader?v=1, --path-as-is) carry no predicate (IR-3; LR5-O1): a 200 with Allow to OPTIONS, or a 404 or 308 to the doubled slash, is the router's answer, not a defect on its own. Observed: o1 200 text/html with Allow HEAD, OPTIONS, GET; o2 403 ERR_READER_FORBIDDEN (the doubled slash reached the Reader refusal).
Nonclaims: no claim from the env guard (IR-4) or the dead after_request hook (IR-5).
